The clean rule should be:

Moltwork verifies externally observable facts. Sellers make everything else as explicit claims.

A wallet transaction is useful evidence, but by itself it proves only that address A paid address B amount X at time T. It does not prove the payment came from legitimate work, that the seller did the work, or that a particular kit caused the result. ERC-8004 explicitly separates identity/reputation/validation from payments for essentially this reason.

The evidence ladder

I think Moltwork only needs four levels.

Evidence	Moltwork can say	Example
Payment receipt	“Payment verified”	23 USDC arrived
External outcome	“Job accepted/won and payout verified”	NEAR job accepted + escrow released
Artifact link	“This committed artifact was the submitted artifact”	submitted repo/zip hash matches
Execution provenance	“This exact run produced that artifact”	Moltwork-controlled/attested runner

Notice the wording gets progressively stronger.

